#: ../../source/docs/common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner.rst:61
#: 425a315b307448f0b70e8c072d0dfa94
msgid "Some boards do not have SD card interfaces for logging, but rather a limited amount of dataflash, typically 16MB. This saves log files in a manner like a circular buffer. Once the flash is filled, the oldest log file is overwritten with the current logging data. If there is only one file on the flash when space runs out, logging is stopped instead."
